# docker/intake.env.example -> copy to docker/intake.env (gitignored) for the intake service
# (compose profile `intake`; security-hardening-2026-10 I5). Loaded by openbrain-intake ONLY
# (`env_file: intake.env`, required: false) - never put intake settings in docker/.env, which
# open_notebook loads whole. The profile is OFF by default; nothing here is used until the
# operator's gated deploy (integrations/intake/README.md, "What I5 ships").
#
# THIS FILE HOLDS NO SECRET (intake-i5b R2-F1). Every `docker exec` process in the container
# (the healthcheck, stack.py health, check-openbrain-health) inherits the container's
# environment, so the three secrets are FILES instead - compose secrets, mounted read-only at
# /run/secrets. The service REFUSES TO START if any of the three secret names below is set in
# its environment (this file included), or if a required file is absent or blank.
#
# The secret files, one value each, no suffix, in docker/intake-secrets/ (gitignored; create the
# directory; a trailing line break is dropped, nothing else):
#   intake_caller_keys         REQUIRED. One key per calling connector, connector=key[,connector=key...];
#                              a key is 32-256 printable characters with no blank, ',' or '='. The
#                              key decides which connector a caller may submit as.
#                                openssl rand -hex 32     (one per connector)
#   intake_db_password         REQUIRED. Password of the `intake` DB role (created by
#                              integrations/intake/sql/init-intake.sql with NO password; the live
#                              apply is a gated deploy step). Set it once on the live DB, the same
#                              value in this file:
#                                psql -U postgres -d openbrain -v ON_ERROR_STOP=1 -v intake_db_password="<value>" -f init-intake.sql
#                                openssl rand -hex 16
#   intake_second_opinion_key  intake's OWN LiteLLM virtual key for the second opinion (metadata.lane
#                              ob-intake; issued in llm-gateway-ui - a gated step). The file must
#                              exist (compose mounts it); EMPTY = unset: every item that needs the
#                              second opinion expires `suspicious`, never clean.
# They are backed up by the nightly config-secrets job (untracked files under a compose secret).

# Screening workers (each ~1.9 GB once loaded) and torch threads per worker.
#INTAKE_CLASSIFIER_WORKERS=1
#INTAKE_CLASSIFIER_THREADS=8
# Operator D40 = (a): clean (default) | suspicious.
#INTAKE_D2_WEAK_RULE_JUDGE_CLEAN=clean
